   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT relating to part-time police officer positions in the villages of Corfu and LeRoy in Genesee county",
    "basePrintNo": "S7553",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7553-2011",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Genesee County",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S7553\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act\nrelating to part-time police officer positions in the villages of Corfu\nand LeRoy in Genesee county\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 This bill would provide that the position of part-time\npolice officer in the villages of Corfu and LeRoy will be deemed\nnon-competitive positions for purposes of Civil Service.\n\nSection 2 provides that this act shall take effect immediately.\n\nPURPOSE AND JUSTIFICATION:\n\nMany years ago, Genesee County enacted\nregulations making the position of part-time police officer a\ncompetitive position within the county.\nThe regulations in surrounding counties, including Livingston, Orleans\nand Wyoming Counties, provide that part-time police officer is a\nnon-competitive position. The Village of Corfu and the Village of\nLeRoy have continuing difficulties finding candidates off the\ncompetitive list who are available when needed for a part-time\nposition. These villages have small police departments, but need\nadditional personnel from time to time, such as when an officer is\nserving in the military reserves or for seasonal demands. The\ncompetitive list is for highly trained and specialized candidates who\noften need over a year of training. Candidates on this list are often\nnot available on a timely basis and may not be interested in a\nposition for what may be only a few hours a week. Also, some of these\npart time positions are effectively seasonal reflecting increased\nneed during certain times of the year. If the position was\nnon-competitive, these villages would be able to reach out to\npart-time police officers in the surrounding counties who are in\nnoncompetitive positions, but experienced and well qualified, to fill\nin needed coverage in LeRoy and Corfu. This bill is supported not\nonly by the Village of Corfu and the Village of LeRoy, but also\nGenesee County, who recognizes the unique difficulties faced by these\ntwo communities within the County.\n\nEXISTING LAW:\n\nCivil Service Law and Regulations provide that an election to make a\nposition competitive is done on a countywide basis.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
